y = a/(1+(N/K)^b), where N is population density and a, b and K are 
parameters which may be linear functions of 'Habitat' and 'Sex'.

To avoid negative values of K I've re-written the function as

y = a/(1+exp(b*log(N) - b*k)), where k=log(K)

As I am new to this kind of models and the use of 'nlme' I've first tried 
to fit the model on a simulated data set. However, i can't get it to work. 
The code I have used to generate the data and fit the model is:

options(contrasts=c(factor="contr.treatment"))

dens.func<-deriv(~a/(1+exp(b*log(N)-b*k)), c("a","b","k"), 
