In an attempt to head off yet more questions about moving compiled library
sections from S+2000 to S+6,

PLEASE note the ReadMe on statlib (and elsewhere)  says

Libraries for S-Plus for Windows
================================

NB.  This collection does not work on S-PLUS 6.0 for Windows.
Some of these are ported to 6.0: see
http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/MASS3/Winlibs/.

Nothing you can do to a library section compiled for S+2000 will make it
work on S+6 short of disassembling the compiled code and the .hlp file.
So please don't ask *me* how to make them work!

The on-line complements to `S Programming' do tell you how to build from
the sources.

