Subject: FW: How to drop unused factor levels in Splus6 (again)?
Message-ID: <0E21AA045067D211A2F300A02461F7A004AB0547@MCDC-ATL-51>

Hi, Bill Dunlap provided that clue that has solved my problem.
After reading chapter 10 of the S+ Programmer's Guide, and some
poking around in the code, I made my own copy of Dr Harrell's
version of the function "[.data.frame". In line 79 I changed

xj <- (if(length(dim(xj)) == 2) xj[i,  , drop = F] else xj[i]);

to

xj <- (if(length(dim(xj)) == 2) xj[i,  , drop = F] else xj[i,drop=T])

Now the unused levels disappear as they did in Splus2000.

Thanks very much to everyone who responded, especially Bill Dunlap
of Insightful and Frank Harrell.

-Bob Byers

