If I understand you correctly, your basic problem is that Hmisc's
subscripting method for factor is not being used.  I haven't looked at
Hmisc recently, but it may be because the subscripting method is not
being installed with setMethod(), as is required for "SV4-style"
methods (Splus6 is based on S version 4, which has a new generic
function/method system.)

Splus 6 is shipped with new-style [ methods for factors and ordered factors:

   > showMethods("[")
         Database                 x
    [1,] "main"   "ANY"
    [2,] "splus"  "Matrix"
    [3,] "splus"  "Surv"
    [4,] "splus"  "data.frame"
    [5,] "splus"  "pframe"
    [6,] "splus"  "factor"
    [7,] "splus"  "ordered"
    ...

and you need to use setMethod to override one of these.  Use something
like
    setMethod("[", "factor", yourfunction, where="Hmisc")
    setMethod("[", "ordered", yourfunction, where="Hmisc")
to install them.  Look at the current methods with getMethod("[","factor"),
etc.  You may find it better to alter them than to install the old Hmisc
[.factor, as some of the rules about default values in methods have
changed.  You need to install the method for factors and ordered
factors since the new-style method-dispatch method doesn't follow the
old-style inheritance.

