From rvaradha at jhsph.edu  Wed Dec  5 03:00:17 2001
From: rvaradha at jhsph.edu (Ravi Varadhan)
Date: Tue, 04 Dec 2001 22:00:17 -0500
Subject: Re: A bug in Splus6
Message-ID: <005701c17d38$f8c0a5a0$70101eac@newmicronpc>

Thanks to David Smith and Nick Ellis for their 
quick responses.

 

They both pointed out that  S-PLUS 6 contains an improvement to "apply" to make it 
run faster, but it doesn't consider the case where the intention of the 
iterating function is to only use the side effects, but not to return any 
value.  

The solution to the problem is to return a value 
such as in the following command:

 

apply(lamda,2,function(x){hist(x,prob=T); lines(density(x)); 1})

 

Best,

Ravi.

