I neglected to tell what desirable property 5 in Hyndman and Fan was
in my previous email (the Splus definition of quantiles does not
satisfy this one but the one that SPSS seems to use and PCTLDEF=4 in
SAS do satisfy it):

Where \hat{Q}_i^{-1}(x) (inverse of quantile definition i) is uniquely defined, 
\hat{Q}_i^{-1}(X_{(1)}) > 0 and \hat{Q}_i^{-1}(X_{(n)}) < 1

"Property P5 reflects the result that for a continuous distribution,
we expect there to be positive probability for values beyond the
range of the data."  (p. 362)

