Therneau.

 

The responses were 
all very instructive, which I greatly appreciated.  Everyone gave the same 
basic answer.  When writing scripts in S-PLUS 6 for Linux, do not put the 
text file in the .Data directory.  It should be in the working directory, 
one directory up from .Data.  The command for running the script is 
source("Script.Name").  Ever since doing this, my scripts have run 
beautifully.  I still contend that this feature is not well documented at 
all, and should be described more explicitly in future 
documentation.

 

Several folks in the 
above list mentioned running S-Plus in the Emacs environment using ESS.  
Gerald Jean sent me a URL to download ESS.  I have not tried it out yet, 
but here is the web site for those interested:

ESS can be found at : http://ess.stat.wisc.edu/pub/

For Emacs, one could start at:

http://www.gnusoftware.com/ilink/ilink.cgi

Happy Monday, 
everyone.

 

