Thanks to Chuck Taylor from Insightful for solving the GA help
mystery.  According to Chuck,

"What you are seeing is the GUI help page for the dialog reached from
the menus as follows:

      Statistics | Regression | Robust MM Linear Regression | Options

This dialog calls lmRobMM, and the discussion refers to the parameters
for lmRobMM.genetic.control.  Incidentally, the parameter names are the
same as those for ltsreg.default."

He adds,

"I can tell you that lmRobMM.genetic.control and lmRob.genetic.control
(in the "robust" library) are the only S-PLUS functions in our
distribution with "[gG]enetic" in their names."

Matt Kurbatt tells us,

 "...about two years back I modified some sections of GA code
from a book available on the web called S-Poetry,
written by (Patrick? not sure about 1st name) Burns."

